  "notes": [
    "Record-only: no quantitative movement or ability expectation is established in docs/behaviour.",
    "Reproduce with recorder seed 12345, pre-staging frame 300, tick zero frame 345, logical cadence 1/30 s; AI suspended and fog revealed.",
    "Observed slots bind the first seven TIE fighters and four TIE bombers created for Empire, without spawning them; their position/facing placeholders do not stage anything. Stop before replenishment; no causal claim about later waves.",
    "Record alive, pos.xyz, fwd.xyz, hull and shield each tick. See README.md for measured usability and reproduction.",
    "Original recordings (P2-06, FoC debug build, quick-loaded map, seed 12345, tick 0 at frame 345): three runs agree bit for bit in every field, so the original's spread is 0. Each tolerance is the larger of that spread and the conversion bound (docs/traces.md): the X-wing and the launched craft move every tick: pos.x stays below 1024 units (to 700), where binary32 steps by 2^-14: 1024 raw; pos.y below 2048 (to 1626), step 2^-13: 2048 raw; pos.z below 256 (craft climb to 167), step 2^-16: 256 raw; the X-wing's hull (from 90) goes off whole numbers below 128, step 2^-17: 128 raw, and its shield (from 20) below 32, step 2^-19: 32 raw; the carrier holds 3000 hull and 600 shield and launched craft take whole-number hits; fwd: yaw and pitch pass non-whole binary32 degrees up to 359.9, where binary32 steps by 2^-15 degree and moves a component by up to 8.94 raw per angle; with the whole-degree terms (2 pi for the remake's turn quanta, 8.5 for its trig, 1 for the recorder's rounding) the bound is 33.66 raw, below 34. Accumulated integration error of the remake's own motion, turning and damage arithmetic is not in these bounds and needs its own evidence."
  ],
  "record_only": true
